{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1843 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "12ce8556ca25ee5015c74cdba6b21b95ae4d7810c8619563bfc35ce5bb55a8b2" :edb/db-before-t 1842 :edb/db-after-t 1843 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535155 50 #inst "2026-10-08T18:12:53.934Z" 13194139535155 true] [17592186133495 1100 "Given that $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf y\\in\\mathbb C^3,$ compute the standard Hermitian inner product $\\langle \\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y} \\rangle$ of the following two vectors.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057166/assets/5d0567f732027d096d674c2513a41a9c32b87c78bb0203d60653d555c8c9a3b9.png)" 13194139535155 true] [17592186133495 1100 "Given that $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf y\\in\\mathbb C^3,$ compute the standard Hermitian inner product $\\langle \\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y} \\rangle$ of the following two vectors.\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}i \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535155 false] [17592186133688 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334273 13194139535155 true] [17592186133688 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334280 13194139535155 true] [17592186133688 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334287 13194139535155 true] [17592186133688 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334294 13194139535155 true] [17592186133688 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334301 13194139535155 true] [17592186133689 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334259 13194139535155 true] [17592186133689 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334315 13194139535155 true] [17592186133788 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334266 13194139535155 true] [17592186133788 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334308 13194139535155 true] [17592186334259 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334260 13194139535155 true] [17592186334259 1089 "q-141160" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334259 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535155 true] [17592186334259 1100 "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- $⟨ia,b⟩=i⟨a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,\\overset{―}{\\alpha }b⟩=⟨\\alpha a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C$\n- $⟨ia,a⟩\\in R$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334259 1113 #uuid "91ad2ee8-eb6d-5323-a363-48d5ab23b581" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334259 1145 "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true.  Indeed, the inner product in ${C}^{n}$ is linear in the first argument. So, a constant multiple from the first argument can be factored out.\n\n- Statement II is true. By the antilinearity of a complex inner product in the second argument and linearity in the first argument, we have \n\n$$\n⟨a,\\overset{―}{\\alpha }b⟩=\\overset{―}{(\\overset{―}{\\alpha })}⟨a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩=⟨\\alpha a,b⟩.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that $⟨a,a⟩\\in R$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}.$ Therefore, if $a\\ne 0,$ then\n\n$$\n⟨ia,a⟩=i⟨a,a⟩\\notin R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334261 13194139535155 true] [17592186334260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334262 13194139535155 true] [17592186334260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334263 13194139535155 true] [17592186334260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334264 13194139535155 true] [17592186334260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334265 13194139535155 true] [17592186334260 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535155 true] [17592186334260 1041 "selection" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334260 1104 #edb/ref 17592186334264 13194139535155 true] [17592186334260 1110 #uuid "a5685e55-d64b-5b7b-8a58-02ad62c79e1e" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334261 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334261 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535155 true] [17592186334261 1111 #uuid "181d6878-54c8-523b-9328-0b0a31098a4b" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334262 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334262 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535155 true] [17592186334262 1111 #uuid "524ac6b3-2e16-535b-86bb-1a3a744dd3ba" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334263 1034 "III only" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334263 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535155 true] [17592186334263 1111 #uuid "617a3510-3ce9-54a9-b908-273b7d5e09b8" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334264 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334264 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535155 true] [17592186334264 1111 #uuid "ae80f021-02b8-513c-87f2-99fa175a06c7" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334265 1034 "II only" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334265 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535155 true] [17592186334265 1111 #uuid "0c9e4dc7-12a7-5d5c-81c5-b582ddd29819" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334266 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334267 13194139535155 true] [17592186334266 1089 "q-141161" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334266 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535155 true] [17592186334266 1100 "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨2a+3b,\\,c⟩$ if \n\n$\\,$ $⟨c,a⟩=2-\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨b,c⟩=1+2\\text{i}.$" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334266 1113 #uuid "d0f3a852-f21d-5ba1-9973-db675afd165e" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334266 1145 "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is linear in the first argument: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨2a+3b,\\,c⟩ & =⟨2a,c⟩+⟨3b,c⟩ \\\\  & =2⟨a,c⟩+3⟨b,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2⟨a,c⟩+3⟨b,c⟩ & =2\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩}+3⟨b,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨c,a⟩$ and $⟨b,c⟩:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩}+3⟨b,c⟩ & =2(\\overset{―}{2-\\text{i}})+3(1+2\\text{i}) \\\\  & =2(2+\\text{i})+3(1+2\\text{i}) \\\\  & =4+2\\text{i}+3+6\\text{i} \\\\  & =7+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334268 13194139535155 true] [17592186334267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334269 13194139535155 true] [17592186334267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334270 13194139535155 true] [17592186334267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334271 13194139535155 true] [17592186334267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334272 13194139535155 true] [17592186334267 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535155 true] [17592186334267 1041 "selection" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334267 1104 #edb/ref 17592186334271 13194139535155 true] [17592186334267 1110 #uuid "50a2b0a5-dc01-5c4b-be7f-8e93bb04a234" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334268 1034 "8+7\\text{i}" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334268 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535155 true] [17592186334268 1111 #uuid "0ffdcda1-c24e-51e4-943d-d5f7ff7f37a5" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334269 1034 "8+\\text{i}" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334269 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535155 true] [17592186334269 1111 #uuid "21a46b06-586d-5437-aaf9-1bb3455accfe" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334270 1034 "7-4\\text{i}" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334270 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535155 true] [17592186334270 1111 #uuid "9bb4f2a1-62fb-51f0-a87d-b802ece00745" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334271 1034 "7+8\\text{i}" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334271 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535155 true] [17592186334271 1111 #uuid "ac56175f-02af-5936-8661-96f49b5d8a21" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334272 1034 "7+4\\text{i}" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334272 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535155 true] [17592186334272 1111 #uuid "d5db2c9e-ec3c-5cd5-95a7-d523056e0a4c" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334273 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334274 13194139535155 true] [17592186334273 1089 "q-43806" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334273 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535155 true] [17592186334273 1100 "Given that $x,y\\in {C}^{4},$ compute the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨x,y⟩$ of the following two vectors.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2i \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -i \\\\ 1 \\\\ i\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334273 1113 #uuid "3589bf59-3ac6-5c59-a90f-136e4c840a92" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334273 1145 "Using the definition of the standard Hermitian inner product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & ={x}_{1}\\overset{―}{{y}_{1}}+{x}_{2}\\overset{―}{{y}_{2}}+{x}_{3}\\overset{―}{{y}_{3}}+{x}_{4}\\overset{―}{{y}_{4}} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\overset{―}{2}+1\\cdot (\\overset{―}{-i})+2i\\cdot \\overset{―}{1}+3\\cdot \\overset{―}{\\,\\text{i}} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot i+2i\\cdot 1+3\\cdot (-\\text{i}) \\\\  & =2+i+2i-3\\text{i} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334275 13194139535155 true] [17592186334274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334276 13194139535155 true] [17592186334274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334277 13194139535155 true] [17592186334274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334278 13194139535155 true] [17592186334274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334279 13194139535155 true] [17592186334274 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535155 true] [17592186334274 1041 "selection" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334274 1104 #edb/ref 17592186334276 13194139535155 true] [17592186334274 1110 #uuid "61d68cb4-9ae0-52c9-984b-7dd175baa217" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334275 1034 "2i" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334275 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535155 true] [17592186334275 1111 #uuid "d304c970-df1a-5b57-b5df-7de4eb02a4d4" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334276 1034 "2" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334276 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535155 true] [17592186334276 1111 #uuid "3c1e1203-7d74-5261-9020-04606cecde28" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334277 1034 "5i" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334277 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535155 true] [17592186334277 1111 #uuid "47f28c12-51f6-512a-989c-7c0f5307b882" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334278 1034 "-2i" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334278 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535155 true] [17592186334278 1111 #uuid "f5d8e6d8-5687-51cf-a37c-60ea2aa91686" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334279 1034 "-2" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334279 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535155 true] [17592186334279 1111 #uuid "1455a7ef-98c3-5f7c-8897-8a7b59c49375" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334280 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334281 13194139535155 true] [17592186334280 1089 "q-43807" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334280 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535155 true] [17592186334280 1100 "Given that $x,y\\in {C}^{3},$ compute the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨x,y⟩$ of the following two vectors.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}i \\\\ i \\\\ i\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}i \\\\ 2 \\\\ -i\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334280 1113 #uuid "159fc2f2-2f72-5d93-b610-2c9c5a129902" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334280 1145 "Using the definition of the standard Hermitian inner product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & ={x}_{1}\\overset{―}{{y}_{1}}+{x}_{2}\\overset{―}{{y}_{2}}+{x}_{3}\\overset{―}{{y}_{3}} \\\\  & =i\\cdot \\overset{―}{\\,i}+i\\cdot \\overset{―}{2}+i\\cdot (\\overset{―}{-\\text{i}}) \\\\  & =i\\cdot (-i)+i\\cdot 2+i\\cdot \\text{i} \\\\  & =1+2i+(-1) \\\\  & =2i.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334281 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334282 13194139535155 true] [17592186334281 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334283 13194139535155 true] [17592186334281 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334284 13194139535155 true] [17592186334281 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334285 13194139535155 true] [17592186334281 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334286 13194139535155 true] [17592186334281 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535155 true] [17592186334281 1041 "selection" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334281 1104 #edb/ref 17592186334282 13194139535155 true] [17592186334281 1110 #uuid "720ee2ab-01e8-5552-b75b-cf8b86c61c6e" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334282 1034 "2i" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334282 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535155 true] [17592186334282 1111 #uuid "2d1889d6-128e-5736-8a4e-4ea5163121ad" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334283 1034 "-1-2i" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334283 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535155 true] [17592186334283 1111 #uuid "13af33f6-be1c-5e55-bf2e-a5dd0b5c6968" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334284 1034 "1-2i" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334284 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535155 true] [17592186334284 1111 #uuid "407c5bdd-9225-517e-8bec-5a6c0aad2529" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334285 1034 "2-i" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334285 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535155 true] [17592186334285 1111 #uuid "d1d157c1-7967-52f9-9c02-0c3169f14907" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334286 1034 "1+2i" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334286 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535155 true] [17592186334286 1111 #uuid "7f66f5f6-ec00-531e-8625-ceb78e08cf64" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334287 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334288 13194139535155 true] [17592186334287 1089 "q-43811" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334287 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535155 true] [17592186334287 1100 "Given that $x,y\\in {C}^{3},$ compute the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨x,y⟩$ of the following two vectors.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}i \\\\ 2i \\\\ -i\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}1+3i \\\\ -i \\\\ -i\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334287 1113 #uuid "f7e903df-f270-55b5-84eb-72ecbe8acae3" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334287 1145 "Using the definition of the standard Hermitian inner product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & ={x}_{1}\\overset{―}{{y}_{1}}+{x}_{2}\\overset{―}{{y}_{2}}+{x}_{3}\\overset{―}{{y}_{3}} \\\\  & =i\\cdot (\\overset{―}{1+3i})+(2i)\\cdot (\\overset{―}{-i})+(-i)\\cdot (\\overset{―}{-i}) \\\\  & =i\\cdot (1-3i)+2i\\cdot i+(-i)\\cdot \\text{i} \\\\  & =(3+i)+(-2)+1 \\\\  & =2+i.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334289 13194139535155 true] [17592186334288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334290 13194139535155 true] [17592186334288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334291 13194139535155 true] [17592186334288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334292 13194139535155 true] [17592186334288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334293 13194139535155 true] [17592186334288 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535155 true] [17592186334288 1041 "selection" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334288 1104 #edb/ref 17592186334293 13194139535155 true] [17592186334288 1110 #uuid "a9b97153-45c1-511f-8210-a7a683ce2aa0" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334289 1034 "-1+2i" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334289 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535155 true] [17592186334289 1111 #uuid "8faf8c5f-d1ac-514b-9d09-8a3eff6123bc" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334290 1034 "-1-2i" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334290 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535155 true] [17592186334290 1111 #uuid "8e774b73-c32d-582b-b065-3b6666b73855" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334291 1034 "1-2i" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334291 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535155 true] [17592186334291 1111 #uuid "51e9554d-be31-516b-bff3-ca1f2a79c123" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334292 1034 "1+i" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334292 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535155 true] [17592186334292 1111 #uuid "04b79595-29a8-575e-9786-db29e3460d66" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334293 1034 "2+i" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334293 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535155 true] [17592186334293 1111 #uuid "e3847b1e-09d4-5464-81e1-df9e5eac96d1" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334294 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334295 13194139535155 true] [17592186334294 1089 "q-43817" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334294 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535155 true] [17592186334294 1100 "Given that $x,y\\in {C}^{3},$ compute the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨x,y⟩$ of the following two vectors.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-1+i \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2-i\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}1+i \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334294 1113 #uuid "03a66baa-aa45-5430-913b-f79634c2af38" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334294 1145 "Using the definition of the standard Hermitian inner product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & ={x}_{1}\\overset{―}{{y}_{1}}+{x}_{2}\\overset{―}{{y}_{2}}+{x}_{3}\\overset{―}{{y}_{3}} \\\\  & =(-1+i)\\cdot (\\overset{―}{1+i})+1\\cdot \\overset{―}{3}+(2-i)\\cdot \\overset{―}{1} \\\\  & =(-1+i)\\cdot (1-i)+1\\cdot 3+(2-i)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2\\text{i}+3+(2-i) \\\\  & =5+i.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535155 true] [17592186334295 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334296 13194139535155 true] [17592186334295 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334297 13194139535155 true] [17592186334295 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334298 13194139535155 true] [17592186334295 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334299 13194139535155 true] [17592186334295 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334300 13194139535155 true] [17592186334295 1040 #edb/ref 17592186